  "ingredients": [
    "1 tablespoon olive oil, or as desired",
    "6 chicken breasts, cut in half lengthwise (butterflied)",
    "salt and ground black pepper to taste",
    "0.75 cup all-purpose flour",
    "1 tablespoon ground paprika",
    "2 large eggs, beaten",
    "2 cups seasoned bread crumbs",
    "1 large lemon, zested"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/IX3G-N0_k7CjGt-O3Uc0WM2xSrU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/244950-baked-chicken-schnitzel-step-1-18-0b7fb5ceb5c5422f8408f46c75a2f313.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/244950/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F (220 degrees C). Line a large baking sheet with aluminum foil; drizzle olive oil over foil. Place the baking sheet in the oven as it preheats.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, place chicken breasts between 2 sheets of plastic wrap on a solid, level surface. Firmly pound with the smooth side of a meat mallet to ¼-inch thickness. Season both sides with salt and black pepper.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine flour and paprika in a shallow bowl. Whisk eggs, salt, and black pepper together in a second shallow bowl. Combine bread crumbs and lemon zest in a third shallow bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/aewVbFXvcFxpxEyuvfGGQoyaY38=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/244950-baked-chicken-schnitzel-step-2-251-4ab605a2f9a14d5891a8f4435c90ef75.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/244950/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dredge 1 piece chicken in flour; shake off excess. Dip into beaten egg. Lift up so excess egg drips back in the bowl. Press into bread crumbs to coat both sides. Place breaded chicken, unstacked, onto a plate. Repeat with remaining chicken.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the baking sheet from the oven. Arrange chicken in a single layer on the hot baking sheet; drizzle more olive oil over each piece.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/tsGji1Ns0fknR5kx6TgrHlAEI84=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/244950-baked-chicken-schnitzel-step-3-27-cda8aebeac5a422183a2d75b68d86e80.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/244950/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven for 5 to 6 minutes. Flip chicken; continue baking until no longer pink in centers and the breading is lightly browned, 5 to 6 minutes more. An instant-read thermometer inserted into centers should read at least 165 degrees F (74 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/n5TbAYtBLCU3cVk0LfApLts10Z0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/244950-baked-chicken-schnitzel-step-4-35-eb70480d775c4f0eb97309eb4107da32.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/244950/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/uaxWo7FvhyDSnBekBaneujCtzXo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/244950-baked-chicken-schnitzel-VAT-Beauty-4x3-2f62a0613f61415e9b62ef0174e0a40b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/244950/step_08.webp"
    }
  ],
